''Slipstream'' (`$:/plugins/mblackman/slipstream`) is a modern, responsive layout theme and UI primitive toolkit for ''TiddlyWiki v5.4.0+''. Designed to stay as close to vanilla TiddlyWiki as possible, Slipstream introduces a clean 3-column workspace, native CSS design tokens, and flexible widgets that power your own custom knowledge workflows without imposing opinions on your data.

---

!! Key Features You Can Test Right Now

# ''Three-Column Desktop Workspace (`>= 1024px`)'':
#* Click `☰` (top-left) to toggle the ''Left Navigation Rail'' (with your pinned notes, recent history, and core tools).
#* Click `◨` (top-right) to toggle the ''Right Context Inspector'', which updates dynamically to show the active tiddler's outline, backlinks, and metadata.
# ''Comfortable Reading Measure with Wide Mode Breakout'':
#* Standard prose notes (like [[Writing & Typography]]) stay centered at an ergonomic `72ch` (`840px`), keeping text distraction-free.
#* Hubs, tables, and dashboards tagged `Wide` (like [[Knowledge Base]] and [[Slipstream UI Primitives]]) automatically expand to `1120px` to fit rich content.
# ''Inline Object Property Pills'':
#* Notice the `status: Active` and `version: 0.1.0` pills right below this tiddler's title! You can configure which fields become pills in [[$:/ControlPanel]] → ''Settings'' → ''Slipstream'', or specify them per-tiddler with the `ss-fields` field.
# ''Mobile Single-Tiddler (`zoomin`) Mode (`< 1024px`)'':
#* Resize your browser window narrower than `1024px` (or open browser device emulation) to experience the mobile zoomin view: an open tiddler pill strip, bottom navigation bar, and slide-up action sheet (`•••`).
# ''Extensible & Native'':
#* Built entirely with TiddlyWiki v5.4.0+ features: `\function`, `\procedure`, `\widget`, `@media`, and `--tpc-*` / `--tp-*` native palette variables.

